<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42071" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπωμ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ʽὦμοσ̓</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the point of the shoulder,</i>
			where it joins the collar-bone, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.10.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				2.273
			</span></i>, etc.; the adjacent part of the collar-bone, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.133
			</span></i> ; acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				493a9
			</span></i>, <i>back part of the neck</i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phgn.</u>
				810b35
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Poet.,
				<i>shoulder,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Achae.
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				143
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.588
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Alc.
			</span></i> Mess.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> part
			of a ship, <i><span class="en">
				Archimel.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.209d
			</span></i> (s.v.l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> in
			pl., <i>leaves</i> of a folding-door, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ez.</u>
				41.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>part of the women's tunic that was fastened on the shoulder by
				brooches, shoulder-strap,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				558
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Chaerem.
				14.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.Car.
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				11(2).287
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				87
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; <i>tunic</i> of a rower, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1404
			</span></i> ; the high-priest's <i>ephod,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				28.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.151
			</span></i>, al.</div>
